::CW_U03_L04_GP_Q01::Central idea: Avoiding responsibility can make guilt grow. Passage detail: Niko hides the baseball under three blankets after blaming the broken window on the wind. How does the detail support the central idea?{
~A. It shows Niko likes blankets.#Incorrect. The blankets matter because he uses them to hide evidence.
~B. It proves the wind broke the window.#Incorrect. The hidden baseball suggests responsibility.
=C. It shows Niko's guilt growing through secretive action.#Correct. The hiding shows avoidance becoming more intense.
~D. It distracts from the central idea completely.#Incorrect. The detail directly supports the idea.
}
::CW_U03_L04_GP_Q02::Central idea: Accepting help can be a form of strength. Which detail best supports the idea?{
=A. The character hands one heavy box to a friend and keeps walking beside her.#Correct. The action shows accepting help without giving up.
~B. The character describes an unrelated poster for three paragraphs.#Incorrect. This does not connect to accepting help.
~C. The character refuses all help and leaves.#Incorrect. This works against the central idea.
~D. The character counts clouds.#Incorrect. This is unrelated unless tied to the conflict.
}
::CW_U03_L04_GP_Q03::Passage: Rae keeps moving an unopened letter into more hidden places. Central idea: Avoiding a hard truth can make fear grow. Which detail is most relevant?{
~A. The wall is painted beige.#Incorrect. This detail does not support the central idea by itself.
~B. Rae owns socks.#Incorrect. This is unrelated.
~C. The day is Tuesday.#Incorrect. The day does not develop the central idea.
=D. Rae hides the letter under a loose floorboard.#Correct. The increasingly secret hiding supports fear and avoidance.
}
::CW_U03_L04_GP_Q04::A draft's central idea is that memory can make a new place feel less lonely. Which revision best supports it?{
~A. Add a random list of every item in the room.#Incorrect. A list is not useful unless details connect to the idea.
=B. Change "blue rug" to "a blue rug the same color as Grandma's kitchen rug."#Correct. The revised detail connects the new place to memory.
~C. Remove every memory detail.#Incorrect. That weakens the central idea.
~D. Add a paragraph about unrelated traffic.#Incorrect. This distracts from the idea.
}
::CW_U03_L04_GP_Q05::Central idea: True confidence includes admitting what you do not know. Which passage detail best supports the idea?{
~A. The character gives a perfect answer and never asks anything.#Incorrect. This does not show admitting uncertainty.
~B. The character changes the topic to lunch.#Incorrect. Avoiding the topic does not support the idea.
=C. The character raises a hand and says, "I need help with the first step."#Correct. The action shows confidence through honest help-seeking.
~D. The character describes the floor tiles only.#Incorrect. That detail is unrelated by itself.
}
